  AUTHORS   Harada,R., Nishimura,Y., Nomura,M., Yabuki,A., Shiba,K., Inaba,K.,
            Inagaki,Y. and Nakayama,T.
  TITLE     A cellular entity retaining only its replicative core: Hidden
            archaeal lineage with an ultra-reduced genome
  JOURNAL   Unpublished
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 238034)
  AUTHORS   Harada,R. and Nakayama,T.
  TITLE     Direct Submission
  JOURNAL   Submitted (18-APR-2025) Contact:Ryo Harada Dalhousie University;
            5850 College Street, Halifax B3H4H7, Canada
COMMENT     Annotated by DFAST https://dfast.ddbj.nig.ac.jp/. This sequence was
            obtained by direct amplification of genomic DNA from prokaryotic
            cells living with Citharistes regius, a dinoflagellate species. A
            Citharistes regius cell (isolate M16) was isolated from a seawater
            sample and the entire cell, including the prokaryotic cells, was
            subjected to whole-genome amplification as a template. The
            amplified products were analyzed on the Illumina NovaSeq 6000
            system and the Oxford Nanopore MinION, and the resulting sequence
            reads were assembled using Unicycler. No contamination from the
            Citharistes regius nuclear genome was detected.
            
